WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:04.364
My mind grew very uneasy on the subject of the pale young gentleman. His bloody nose had

2
00:00:04.365 --> 00:00:09.356
stained my trousers, and I tried to wash out the evidence in the dead of night. For days

3
00:00:09.357 --> 00:00:14.523
I kept close to home, fearing that the officers of the county jail would pounce upon me.

4
00:00:14.524 --> 00:00:19.349
When the day arrived for my return to the scene of the crime, my terrors reached their

5
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:26.602
height. But nothing happened! No one mentioned it, and no pale young gentleman was to be found

6
00:00:26.603 --> 00:00:36.515
when I looked in the windows of the small house. I entered the main house. In the passage

7
00:00:36.516 --> 00:00:40.261
between Miss Havisham's room and the room with the wedding cake, I saw a garden chair—a light

8
00:00:40.262 --> 00:00:44.999
chair on wheels that was pushed from behind. On that day I began the task of pushing

9
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.840
Miss Havisham in the chair. We went around her room, across the passage, and around the other room.

10
00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:55.253
Over and over we made this journey, often for as long as three hours at a time.

11
00:00:55.254 --> 00:01:01.563
It was decided that I should return every other day, and I did this for the next

12
00:01:01.564 --> 00:01:04.301
eight to ten months. As we grew more used to each other, Miss Havisham began to ask me

13
00:01:04.302 --> 00:01:13.738
questions about what I had learned and what I was going to be. I told her that

14
00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:17.485
I was to be apprenticed to Joe. I also said that I knew nothing but wanted to

15
00:01:17.486 --> 00:01:24.118
know everything, hoping she might help me learn. But she never did. Nor did she ever pay

16
00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:28.207
me for my visits. Estella was always there but never told me I might kiss her again. Sometimes

17
00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:36.293
she coldly tolerated me; sometimes she was quite nice to me; sometimes she told me she hated

18
00:01:36.294 --> 00:01:41.714
me. I was often puzzled by her moods and didn't know what to say or do. At

19
00:01:41.715 --> 00:01:47.952
those times Miss Havisham would embrace Estella and whisper something to her that sounded like: "Break men's hearts

20
00:01:47.953 --> 00:01:51.873
and have no mercy!" Miss Havisham often whispered to me too. "Does she grow prettier and prettier,

21
00:01:51.874 --> 00:01:56.866
Pip?" And she seemed delighted when I said, "Yes." For Estella did grow more beautiful every day.

22
00:01:56.867 --> 00:02:03.595
And so we continued to play cards and walk around the gloomy rooms. I never told Joe

23
00:02:03.596 --> 00:02:08.349
about the pale young gentleman or about anything that went on at Miss Havisham's. But I told Biddy

24
00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:13.016
everything. I didn't understand until much later why I confided in her and why she listened to

25
00:02:13.017 --> 00:02:17.349
me. Meanwhile Mr. Pumblechook often came in the evenings to discuss my future with my sister. The

26
00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:22.921
two of them would speculate for hours about what Miss Havisham was going to do for me. This

27
00:02:22.922 --> 00:02:24.691
made me so angry that I wanted to burst into tears and hit Mr. Pumblechook. One day

28
00:02:24.692 --> 00:02:32.746
when I was at Miss Havisham's, she said, "Tell me again the name of your blacksmith." "Joe

29
00:02:32.747 --> 00:02:35.341
Gargery, ma'am." "You are growing up, Pip. You should be apprenticed at once. Would Gargery come here and

30
00:02:35.342 --> 00:02:37.675
bring your indenture papers?" "He would see it as an honor to be asked." "Then tell him

31
00:02:37.676 --> 00:02:43.580
to come here with you." When I went home that night and delivered this message for Joe,

32
00:02:43.581 --> 00:02:50.580
my sister went on the worst rampage I'd ever seen. "What am I—a doormat under your feet?"

33
00:02:50.581 --> 00:02:55.802
she asked Joe and me. "Am I not good enough for Miss Havisham?" Then she heaved a candlestick

34
00:02:55.803 --> 00:02:59.961
at Joe, burst into loud sobbing, and began furiously cleaning. She took up her bucket and scrub

35
00:02:59.962 --> 00:03:05.644
brush and threw Joe and me out of the house. We stood shivering in the backyard until

36
00:03:05.645 --> 00:03:09.636
ten o'clock when we determined it was safe to come inside. Two days later Joe shut up the

37
00:03:09.637 --> 00:03:13.723
forge for the day and put on his best clothes. I should have told him that he

38
00:03:13.724 --> 00:03:20.477
looked much more comfortable in his everyday clothes. My sister insisted on accompanying us to town. She

39
00:03:20.478 --> 00:03:25.382
stayed with Mr. Pumblechook while we walked on to Miss Havisham's. Estella led us up to Miss

40
00:03:25.383 --> 00:03:34.882
Havisham's room, where Miss Havisham was seated at her dressing table. "Well," she said to Joe, "you have

41
00:03:34.883 --> 00:03:41.191
raised this boy with the intention of making him your apprentice. Does he like the trade? Has

42
00:03:41.192 --> 00:03:46.699
he ever made any objections?" "You know, Pip," Joe said to me, "since we are the best

43
00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:51.032
of friends, I'd have paid attention if you'd made objections." I tried to signal to him that it

44
00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:54.532
was proper to talk to Miss Havisham and not to me, but it did no good. "Did

45
00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:59.921
you bring his indenture papers with you?" asked Miss Havisham. "Oh, Pip! You know you saw me

46
00:03:59.922 --> 00:04:04.350
put them in my hat this morning." With that he handed me the papers. I'm sorry to say

47
00:04:04.351 --> 00:04:07.667
I was ashamed of the dear, good fellow. I felt even more ashamed when I saw that

48
00:04:07.668 --> 00:04:15.501
Estella was silently laughing at him. I gave the papers to Miss Havisham and she looked them

49
00:04:15.502 --> 00:04:18.993
over. "Pip has earned some money, and here it is." She picked up a little bag from

50
00:04:18.994 --> 00:04:22.667
the table. "Give this to your master, Pip." I handed the bag to Joe, and he persisted in

51
00:04:22.668 --> 00:04:28.913
talking to me. "This is very liberal on your part, Pip, and I am most grateful." "Good-bye,

52
00:04:28.914 --> 00:04:30.746
Pip," said Miss Havisham, handing us back the papers. "Let them out, Estella." "Am I to come

53
00:04:30.747 --> 00:04:40.143
again, ma'am?" "No, Gargery is your master now. And Gargery, that 25 pounds is Pip’s reward. Don't expect

54
00:04:40.144 --> 00:04:42.643
anything more from me." We went on to Mr. Pumblechook's house. "Well," said my sister, "It's a

55
00:04:42.644 --> 00:04:48.738
wonder that you two have come back to such poor society as this." "Miss Havisham," said Joe,

56
00:04:48.739 --> 00:04:55.555
"made a great effort to say we should give her compliments to you. Isn't that right, Pip?"

57
00:04:55.556 --> 00:05:01.048
"Oh yes." I immediately realized that he was making this all up to please my sister. "She said,"

58
00:05:01.049 --> 00:05:07.714
Joe went on, "that she wished the state of her health allowed her the pleasure of having

59
00:05:07.715 --> 00:05:13.706
ladies visit." "Well." My sister gave a satisfied glance at Mr. Pumblechook. "And what did she give

60
00:05:13.707 --> 00:05:22.293
Pip?" "She gave him nothing," said Joe. Before my sister could explode, he continued. "But to his family,

61
00:05:22.294 --> 00:05:26.103
she gave this 25 pounds." My sister immediately grabbed the money from Joe's hands. Then Mr. Pumblechook

62
00:05:26.104 --> 00:05:29.611
said I must be bound at once to Joe. And so we left for the town hall,

63
00:05:29.612 --> 00:05:34.778
where we signed the papers officially making me Joe's apprentice. Once I had believed in the blacksmith's forge

64
00:05:34.779 --> 00:05:39.922
as the glowing road to manhood and independence. I had felt that when I at last rolled

65
00:05:39.923 --> 00:05:46.684
up my sleeves and went to work as Joe's apprentice, I would be distinguished and happy. But

66
00:05:46.685 --> 00:05:51.605
within a single year, everything changed, and the forge seemed coarse and common. It's a dreadful thing

67
00:05:51.606 --> 00:05:54.343
to feel ashamed of home. What I feared most was that someday, when I was at my dirtiest,

68
00:05:54.344 --> 00:06:02.389
I would lift up my eyes from my work and see Estella looking in through the window.

